# Backend Route Rules

## Authentication — Always First

```javascript
const userId = await getUserId(req); // from ./auth.js — already imported in server.js
if (!userId) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });
```

Every non-public endpoint must authenticate before touching data.

## Route Structure Template

```javascript
app.get('/api/my-feature', async (req, res) => {
  try {
    const userId = await getUserId(req);
    if (!userId) return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' });

    const data = await db.myFeatureGet(userId);
    res.json(data);
  } catch (err) {
    console.error('GET /api/my-feature error:', err);
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' });
  }
});
```

## Database Abstraction

Use `db.*` methods — NEVER query PostgreSQL directly in `server.js`:
```javascript
const db = require('./db'); // already required at top of server.js
```

When adding a new storage function, implement it in **both**:
- `backend/src/storage_pg.js` — PostgreSQL implementation
- `backend/src/storage.js` — JSON file fallback (same signature)

## Input Validation

```javascript
const { field1, field2 } = req.body;
if (!field1) return res.status(400).json({ error: 'field1 is required' });
if (typeof field1 !== 'string') return res.status(400).json({ error: 'field1 must be a string' });
```

- Validate all `req.body`, `req.params`, and `req.query` fields
- Use parameterised queries — never interpolate user input into SQL
- Limit string lengths before DB insertion

## SQL Migrations

New table or column needed → create `backend/src/migrations/NNN_description.sql`:
- Use next sequential number (currently up to `020`)
- Use `IF NOT EXISTS` — migrations must be idempotent
- Run with `node src/migrate.js`
- Never edit existing migration files

## Error Logging

```javascript
console.error('METHOD /api/route error:', err);
```

Never expose stack traces or internal error details in the response body.

## CORS & Middleware

Configured globally — do not add per-route CORS headers.

## Admin Routes

```javascript
// Check admin before proceeding
const user = await db.getUser(userId);
if (!user?.is_admin) return res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' });
```

## File Uploads

Use the existing `multer` configuration in `server.js` — do not add a new multer instance.
Use `sharp` (already imported) for any image processing.

## Response Conventions

| Situation | Response |
|---|---|
| Success | `res.json(data)` or `res.json({ ok: true })` |
| Not found | `res.status(404).json({ error: 'Not found' })` |
| Bad request | `res.status(400).json({ error: 'Descriptive message' })` |
| Unauthorised | `res.status(401).json({ error: 'Unauthorized' })` |
| Forbidden | `res.status(403).json({ error: 'Forbidden' })` |
| Server error | `res.status(500).json({ error: 'Internal server error' })` |
